# The windowed conformance scene (docs/virtualization-plan.md §6.3):
# the ONE scene that exercises a real narrowed band on all five lanes,
# because its guest is compiled (guests/rust/windowed.rs) where
# ledger/varied are Python and stop at the desktops. 400 uniform rows
# in a grown table overflow every tier's band; the guest writes no
# windowing code.
#
# expect_window says the FIRST VISIBLE row and the DECLARED TOTAL,
# both data (ruled 2026-08-25); after scroll_to_row the first visible
# row IS the scrolled-to row. Every number here is data; the band's
# width belongs to the core's tests and the table-tier probe.
expect_columns column#0 "Name|Size"
expect_column_edges column#0 2
# The whole collection is data behind a band of widgets.
expect_window column#0 0 400
# Deep by identity: a row no tier should have realized yet.
scroll_to_row column#0 r200
expect_window column#0 200 400
# Back: membership is arithmetic, not history — byte-identical to the
# opening line on every platform.
scroll_to_row column#0 r000
expect_window column#0 0 400
